{"timestamp": "2026-06-13T14:34:56", "domain": "medical_prescription", "query": "What is Amoxicillin", "original_answer": "# Common Medications and Medical Conditions Guide ## Overview This guide provides evidence-based information about common medications and medical conditions. Always consult a qualified healthcare provider before starting, stopping, or changing any medication. --- ## Pain and Fever Medications ### Paracetamol (Acetaminophen) **Brand Names**: Tylenol, Panadol, Calpol **Uses**: - Relieve mild to moderate pain (headaches, toothaches, muscle aches) - Reduce fever **Dosage**: - Adults: 500-1000mg every 4-6 hours, maximum 4000mg per day - Children: Based on weight, usually 10-15mg/kg every 4-6 hours **Side Effects**: - Rare at recommended doses - Overdose can cause liver damage **Warnings**: - Do not take more than 4000mg in 24 hours - Avoid alcohol while taking paracetamol - Check other medications for paracetamol to avoid accidental overdose ### Ibuprofen **Brand Names**: Advil, Motrin, Nurofen **Uses**: - Relieve pain and inflammation (arthritis, sprains, headaches) - Reduce fever **Dosage**: - Adults: 200-400mg every 4-6 hours, maximum 1200mg per day **Side Effects**: - Stomach pain or indigestion - Nausea - Dizziness **Warnings**: - Take with food or milk to reduce stomach upset - Long-term use can increase risk of heart attack or stroke - Not recommended for people with stomach ulcers, kidney problems, or heart disease ### Aspirin **Brand Names**: Bayer, Ecotrin **Uses**: - Relieve pain and inflammation - Reduce fever - Low-dose (75-100mg daily) for heart attack and stroke prevention in at-risk individuals **Dosage**: - Pain relief: 325-650mg every 4-6 hours - Heart health: 75-100mg once daily (only as directed by doctor) **Side Effects**: - Stomach irritation - Increased risk of bleeding **Warnings**: - Do not give to children or teenagers (risk of Reye's syndrome) - Avoid with blood thinners unless directed by doctor --- ## Allergy Medications ### Cetirizine **Brand Names**: Zyrtec, Reactine **Uses**: - Relieve hay fever symptoms (sneezing, runny nose, itchy eyes) - Relieve allergic skin reactions (hives, itching) **Dosage**: - Adults and children over 12: 10mg once daily - Children 6-12: 5-10mg once daily **Side Effects**: - Drowsiness (less than older antihistamines) - Dry mouth - Headache **Warnings**: - May cause drowsiness in some people; avoid driving until you know how it affects you - Avoid alcohol ### Loratadine **Brand Names**: Claritin, Alavert **Uses**: - Relieve hay fever symptoms - Relieve hives and itching **Dosage**: - Adults and children over 6: 10mg once daily **Side Effects**: - Headache - Dry mouth - Fatigue **Warnings**: - Generally non-drowsy at recommended doses --- ## Heartburn and Acid Reflux Medications ### Omeprazole **Brand Names**: Prilosec, Losec **Uses**: - Treat heartburn and acid reflux - Treat and prevent stomach and duodenal ulcers - Treat GERD (Gastroesophageal Reflux Disease) **Dosage**: - Heartburn: 20mg once daily for 4-8 weeks - Maintenance: 20mg once daily or 10mg once daily **Side Effects**: - Headache - Stomach pain - Nausea - Diarrhea **Warnings**: - Long-term use (over 1 year) may increase risk of bone fractures, C. difficile infection, or low magnesium - Take 30-60 minutes before food ### Ranitidine **Brand Names**: Zantac **Uses**: - Relieve heartburn and indigestion - Treat and prevent ulcers **Note**: Many brands have been withdrawn due to potential contamination **Side Effects**: - Headache - Dizziness - Constipation or diarrhea --- ## High Blood Pressure Medications ### Amlodipine **Brand Names**: Norvasc **Uses**: - Treat high blood pressure (hypertension) - Treat angina (chest pain) **Dosage**: - Adults: 5-10mg once daily **Side Effects**: - Swelling of ankles or feet - Dizziness - Headache - Fatigue **Warnings**: - May cause dizziness when standing up quickly (orthostatic hypotension) ### Lisinopril **Brand Names**: Zestril, Prinivil **Uses**: - Treat high blood pressure - Treat heart failure - Improve survival after heart attack **Dosage**: - Hypertension: 10-40mg once daily **Side Effects**: - Dry cough (common) - Dizziness - Headache - High potassium levels **Warnings**: - Do not take if pregnant or breastfeeding - May cause allergic reactions (rare but serious) --- ## Diabetes Medications ### Metformin **Brand Names**: Glucophage, Glumetza **Uses**: - Treat type 2 diabetes - First-line treatment for type 2 diabetes **Dosage**: - 500mg twice daily or 850mg once daily, gradually increased as needed **Side Effects**: - Stomach upset (nausea, vomiting, diarrhea) - Metallic taste in mouth **Warnings**: - Take with food to reduce stomach upset - Rare but serious risk of lactic acidosis (seek medical help immediately if you have muscle pain, trouble breathing, or unusual tiredness) ### Insulin **Uses**: - Treat type 1 diabetes - Treat type 2 diabetes when other medications aren't enough **Types**: - Rapid-acting (insulin aspart, insulin lispro) - Short-acting (regular insulin) - Intermediate-acting (NPH insulin) - Long-acting (insulin glargine, insulin detemir) **Side Effects**: - Low blood sugar (hypoglycemia) \u2013 symptoms include shaking, sweating, hunger, confusion, dizziness - Injection site reactions **Warnings**: - Learn to recognize and treat low blood sugar immediately - Always check blood sugar levels regularly - Rotate injection sites --- ## Antibiotics ### Amoxicillin **Brand Names**: Amoxil **Uses**: - Treat bacterial infections (ear infections, sinus infections, pneumonia, urinary tract infections) **Dosage**: - Adults: 250-500mg every 8 hours or 500-875mg every 12 hours **Side Effects**: - Nausea - Vomiting - Diarrhea - Rash **Warnings**: - Complete the full course even if you feel better - May reduce effectiveness of birth control pills - Do not take if allergic to penicillin ### Azithromycin **Brand Names**: Zithromax **Uses**: - Treat bacterial infections (chest infections, ear infections, skin infections) - Single-dose option for some infections **Dosage**: - 500mg once daily for 3-5 days **Side Effects**: - Stomach upset - Nausea - Diarrhea - Headache **Warnings**: - Take on empty stomach for better absorption - May cause heart rhythm problems in rare cases --- ## Mental Health Medications ### Sertraline **Brand Names**: Zoloft **Uses**: - Treat depression - Treat anxiety disorders (GAD, OCD, panic disorder, PTSD) - Treat social anxiety disorder **Dosage**: - Depression/anxiety: 50-200mg once daily **Side Effects**: - Nausea - Headache - Insomnia or drowsiness - Sexual side effects - Weight changes **Warnings**: - May take 4-6 weeks to feel full effect - Do not stop suddenly (risk of withdrawal symptoms) - Increased risk of suicidal thoughts in young adults (monitor closely) ### Fluoxetine **Brand Names**: Prozac **Uses**: - Treat depression - Treat OCD - Treat bulimia nervosa - Treat panic disorder **Dosage**: - Depression: 20-80mg once daily **Side Effects**: - Nausea - Headache - Insomnia - Sexual side effects **Warnings**: - Same as sertraline --- ## Common Medical Conditions ### Fever **What is it?**: Elevated body temperature, usually above 38\u00b0C (100.4\u00b0F) **Causes**: - Infections (viral or bacterial) - Inflammatory conditions - Vaccinations **Home Care**: - Stay hydrated - Rest - Paracetamol or ibuprofen (if appropriate) to reduce fever and discomfort **When to see a doctor**: - Fever in infants under 3 months - Fever over 40\u00b0C (104\u00b0F) - Fever lasting more than 3 days in children or 5 days in adults - Symptoms like difficulty breathing, chest pain, confusion, stiff neck ### Headache **Types**: Tension-type headaches (most common) - Do not take if pregnant or breastfeeding - May cause allergic reactions (rare but serious) --- ## Diabetes Medications ### Metformin **Brand Names**: Glucophage, Glumetza **Uses**: - Treat type 2 diabetes - First-line treatment for type 2 diabetes **Dosage**: - 500mg twice daily or 850mg once daily, gradually increased as needed **Side Effects**: - Stomach upset (nausea, vomiting, diarrhea) - Metallic taste in mouth **Warnings**: - Take with food to reduce stomach upset - Rare but serious risk of lactic acidosis (seek medical help immediately if you have muscle pain, trouble breathing, or unusual tiredness) ### Insulin **Uses**: - Treat type 1 diabetes - Treat type 2 diabetes when other medications aren't enough **Types**: - Rapid-acting (insulin aspart, insulin lispro) - Short-acting (regular insulin) - Intermediate-acting (NPH insulin) - Long-acting (insulin glargine, insulin detemir) **Side Effects**: - Low blood sugar (hypoglycemia) \u2013 symptoms include shaking, sweating, hunger, confusion, dizziness - Injection site reactions **Warnings**: - Learn to recognize and treat low blood sugar immediately - Always check blood sugar levels regularly - Rotate injection sites --- ## Antibiotics ### Amoxicillin **Brand Names**: Amoxil **Uses**: - Treat bacterial infections (ear infections, sinus infections, pneumonia, urinary tract infections) **Dosage**: - Adults: 250-500mg every 8 hours or 500-875mg every 12 hours **Side Effects**: - Nausea - Vomiting - Diarrhea - Rash **Warnings**: - Complete the full course even if you feel better - May reduce effectiveness of birth control pills - Do not take if allergic to penicillin ### Azithromycin **Brand Names**: Zithromax **Uses**: - Treat bacterial infections (chest infections, ear infections, skin infections) - Single-dose option for some infections **Dosage**: - 500mg once daily for 3-5 days **Side Effects**: - Stomach upset - Nausea - Diarrhea - Headache **Warnings**: - Take on empty stomach for better absorption - May cause heart rhythm problems in rare cases --- ## Mental Health Medications ### Sertraline **Brand Names**: Zoloft **Uses**: - Treat depression - Treat anxiety disorders (GAD, OCD, panic disorder, PTSD) - Treat social anxiety disorder **Dosage**: - Depression/anxiety: 50-200mg once daily **Side Effects**: